// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 14-control-flow
// facility: rule.control.flow-analysis closure row; rule.fn.closure [Closure-Form-Borrow]; D-0243; conf.ref-captured-by-closure-then-reassigned
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.aliasing-conflict (dynamic)
//
// The closure writes through the reference `r`, so it captures `r` itself by
// an exclusive borrow. Reassigning `r` while the closure lives meets that
// borrow. The closure row formed no fact for a capture of reference type, so
// before D-0243 the table proved the write to `r` clash-free (the model's
// `model.proven-but-false`); it now marks `r` escaped, and the write is
// checked. Both tools always checked it.

import std;

fn main()
{
    i32 x = 1;
    i32 y = 2;
    {
        auto r = &mut x;
        auto c = [r]() { *r = *r + 1; };
        r = &mut y;
        c();
    }
    printf("%v %v\n", x, y);
}
